{"paper": "RRB-RPF-Constable-12-Mar-2025-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 120, "tagged_count": 35, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The sum of 8 numbers is 948. Find their average.", "options": [{"text": "116.5", "added": false}, {"text": "118.5", "added": false}, {"text": "117.5", "added": false}, {"text": "119.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "118.5"}, {"n": 2, "text": "The average of first 124 even numbers is", "options": [{"text": "126", "added": false}, {"text": "125", "added": false}, {"text": "124.5", "added": false}, {"text": "125.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": "125"}, {"n": 3, "text": "What will be the compound interest (in ₹) on a sum of ₹30,000 after two years at a rate of 16% per annum compounded annually?", "options": [{"text": "10,386", "added": false}, {"text": "10,638", "added": false}, {"text": "10,368", "added": false}, {"text": "10,683", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "10,368"}, {"n": 4, "text": "The monthly incomes of two friends Kiran and Mahesh, are in the ratio 5 : 7 respectively and each of them saves ₹78000 every month. If the ratio of their monthly expenditure is 1 : 3, find the monthly income of Kiran(in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "98500", "added": false}, {"text": "97500", "added": false}, {"text": "96500", "added": false}, {"text": "136500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "97500"}, {"n": 5, "text": "Simplify the given expression.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A bus travelling at 100 km/h completes a journey in 17 hours. At what speed will it have to cover the same distance in 5 hours?", "options": [{"text": "344 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "332 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "347 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "340 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "340 km/h"}, {"n": 7, "text": "The marked price of a juicer is ₹7,500. The store offers a 15% discount. What is the price (in ₹) after the discount?", "options": [{"text": "6,335", "added": false}, {"text": "6,357", "added": false}, {"text": "6,735", "added": false}, {"text": "6,375", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "6,375"}, {"n": 8, "text": "Find the value of 2.54 × 0.4 − 0.58 × 5.64 + 2.85 × 3.14 − 0.84 + 4.8 × 3.8 − 7.0938.", "options": [{"text": "21.58", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "23.67", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "17"}, {"n": 9, "text": "The perimeter of one face of a cube is 36 cm. What is its volume?", "options": [{"text": "314 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "243 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "942 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "729 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "729 cm 3"}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "36436", "added": false}, {"text": "32654", "added": false}, {"text": "34663", "added": false}, {"text": "35456", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": "36436"}, {"n": 11, "text": "The value of", "options": [{"text": "983", "added": false}, {"text": "984", "added": false}, {"text": "981", "added": false}, {"text": "982", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "981"}, {"n": 12, "text": "Which of the following ratio is smallest?", "options": [{"text": "17 : 40", "added": false}, {"text": "26 : 53", "added": false}, {"text": "15 : 60", "added": false}, {"text": "11 : 34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "15 : 60"}, {"n": 13, "text": "Shifa can do a certain piece of work in 18 days. Shifa and Afiya can together do the same work in 14 days, and Shifa, Afiya and Mariyam can do the same work together in 9 days. In how many days can Shifa and Mariyam do the same work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A can do a piece of work in 12 days. B can do it in 20 days. With the assistance of C, they completed the work in 3 days. C alone can do it in ______________days.", "options": [{"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "5"}, {"n": 15, "text": "A sum, when invested at 10% simple interest per annum, amounts to ₹2880 after 2 years. What is the simple interest (in ₹) on the same sum at the same rate of interest in 1 year?", "options": [{"text": "960", "added": false}, {"text": "240", "added": false}, {"text": "480", "added": false}, {"text": "120", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "240"}, {"n": 16, "text": "The price of edible oil is increased by 30%. To maintain the budget, Reena reduces the consumption of this oil by 18%. Find the increased percentage in expenditure due to this edible oil.", "options": [{"text": "6.9%", "added": false}, {"text": "6.6%", "added": false}, {"text": "6.3%", "added": false}, {"text": "6.1%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "6.6%"}, {"n": 17, "text": "A dealer purchased a washing machine for ₹15,700. He allows a discount of 16% on its marked price and still makes a profit of 20%. Find the marked price (nearest in ₹) of the washing machine.", "options": [{"text": "₹22,249", "added": false}, {"text": "₹22,942", "added": false}, {"text": "₹22,492", "added": false}, {"text": "₹22,429", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹22,429"}, {"n": 18, "text": "Shaurya has to reach Indore which is 652 km away in 18 hours. His starting speed for 3 hours was 73 km/hr. For the next 134 km his speed was 67km/hr. By what speed he must travel now so as to reach Indore in decided time of 18hours?", "options": [{"text": "23 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "26 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "18 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "20 km/hr", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "23 km/hr"}, {"n": 19, "text": "The present cost of a apartment is ₹152629. After a year, its cost increased to ₹186783. The percentage increase (rounded off to the nearest integer) in the cost of the apartment is:", "options": [{"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "22"}, {"n": 20, "text": "A car travels 272 km in the first hour and 294 km in the second hour. What is the average speed (in km/h) of the car for the whole journey?", "options": [{"text": "293", "added": false}, {"text": "2